	"data": "Concept: Nanolucent — Light-Based Spatial Unit\n\n\"Maybe try to use light. Nanoseconds. One nano-lucent.\" — cithoreal, May 2026\n\nDefinition\n\n1 nano-lucent (nL) = 1 light-nanosecond ≈ 29.98 cm ≈ 11.8 inches\n\nA spatial unit based on the distance light travels in one nanosecond. Conveniently close to 1 foot, making it intuitive for room-scale measurements while being physically grounded in the speed of light.\n\nWhy\n\nFor Room 2.0's coordinate system, spatial computing deserves spatial units. Rather…",
